  "transform": "compact the bars into the output border; place the normalized mask inside it; recolor each mask pixel by the color of its unique nearest border side, leaving tied pixels as the mask color",
  "grid_shape": "n+2 by n+2, where n is the side-bar length and mask bbox size"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 14-16 rows x 15-16 cols, background 0
  frame:
    shape: 4 solid bars (top, bottom, left, right) each length n, width 1
    n: 3-5
    layout: forms (n+2)x(n+2) rectangle; corners are background; interior all background
    colors: 4 distinct non-zero non-8 colors, one per side
  mask:
    color: always 8
    bbox: exactly n x n, matching frame interior size
    density: 0.62-0.67 of n*n cells filled
    symmetry: none [observed]
    connectivity: may be 1-4 connected components (4-conn)
    constraint: must have both tied and unique-nearest-side pixels (>=1 each)
  separation: frame and mask bboxes do not overlap (min Chebyshev distance >=3)
  output:
    size: (n+2) x (n+2)
    border: 4 bars placed on edges, corners background
    interior: mask normalized into interior; each mask pixel recolored by its unique nearest side color (top/left/bottom/right by row/col distance to edge); tied-distance pixels stay color 8

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick n in 3-5. Pick background=0, mask_color=8, and 4 distinct side colors from 1-7 minus 8.
    2. Build the (n+2)x(n+2) output frame with 4 colored bars on edges, bg corners.
    3. Generate a random n x n binary mask with density ~0.6-0.7. Ensure at least 1 pixel has a unique nearest side and at least 1 pixel is equidistant to >=2 sides.
    4. Apply the nearest-side recoloring rule to fill the output interior.
    5. Build input grid (14-16 x 15-16). Place the 4 frame bars in their open-rectangle layout (corners=bg, interior=bg) at a random position. Place the raw mask (all 8s) at a separate non-overlapping position with >=3 Chebyshev gap from frame bbox.
